Experiment No.: 6

Title

Demonstration of Digital I/O Functions

Aim

To demonstrate digital input and output functions of Arduino.

Theory

Digital pins of Arduino can be configured as INPUT or OUTPUT. Digital input reads signals from sensors or switches, while digital output controls devices like LEDs.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
LED
Push Button
220Ω Resistor
Breadboard
Jumper Wires
Procedure
Connect LED to digital pin 13.
Connect push button to digital pin 2.
Set LED as OUTPUT and button as INPUT.
Upload the program.
Press the button and observe LED operation.
Code
int led = 13;
int button = 2;

void setup()
{
  pinMode(led, OUTPUT);
  pinMode(button, INPUT_PULLUP);
}

void loop()
{
  if(digitalRead(button)==LOW)
    digitalWrite(led,HIGH);
  else
    digitalWrite(led,LOW);
}
Output

LED turns ON when the button is pressed.

Result

Digital input and output functions were demonstrated successfully.

Conclusion

Arduino digital I/O operations were studied successfully.
